## Final Judgement
Based on the fact-check, the key finding is that an 18-year-old BJP supporter named Trilochan Mahato was found dead in Purulia, West Bengal, on May 30, 2018. A handwritten note found on his body stated the killing was punishment for supporting BJP, and the BJP party accused the TMC. However, police classified the death as suicide, and no individuals officially confirmed to be TMC workers were identified as perpetrators. The incident occurred over two years before the claim date of October 13, 2020.

The evidence does not support the claim that the killing happened "recently" (relative to the claim date), and it does not provide clear confirmation that the perpetrators were officially TMC workers, as this remains an accusation rather than an established fact in the records reviewed.

Therefore, the claim contains elements that are not fully supported by the documented evidence, specifically the recency and the confirmed identity of the perpetrators as TMC workers. The final decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The fact-check refutes the claim, as the incident refers to the death of 18-year-old BJP supporter Trilochan Mahato in Purulia, West Bengal, on [May 30, 2018](https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/another-man-found-hanging-in-bengal-village-bjp-claims-its-worker-1248550-2018-06-02). While a [note found on his body](https://organiser.org/2018/05/31/120676/bharat/this-is-for-doing-bjp-politics/) stated it was punishment for supporting BJP and the party accused the TMC, police classified the death as [suicide](https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kolkata/bjp-workers-death-due-to-suicide-police-says/articleshow/64435518.cms), and no individuals officially confirmed as TMC workers were identified as perpetrators. The event occurred over two years before the claim's date of October 13, 2020, making it not "recent."